I sent you an email reply, but a general response may be useful:

Segfaults and other game crashes are generally bugs in NetHack itself, 
so we try to collect whatever we can from crash reports so we can file 
bug reports whenever possible.  So, whatever you remember that may be 
relevant (and terminal captures if possible) can be really good for 
that.  Matthew's email report was good, but probably not enough to try 
to replicate and file a bug.  In fairness, it's often not possible to 
get enough info after a crash anyway.

At the very least, please include the server name, your player name and 
the control server's clock time (available on the page at 
<http://nethack.devnull.net>) when sending in a crash report.  We need 
all three of these in order to identify possibly appropriate backup 
files to restore in the event that the crash left no usable lock files.

It's also useful to know whatever you can recall about character level 
and dungeon level, since those can pretty precisely identify the most 
appropriate session backup (since both often change between sessions and 
character level _usually_ only goes up).

Essentially, whatever you recall of the game leading up to a crash (and 
can summon the inspiration to actually type up on the off chance that 
it'd be useful) would be a good idea in any crash report you email us.

Thanks,
